== status line ==
minimal: Done version=Http11 code=200 reason="OK" headers=0 consumed=19
http/1.0: Done version=Http10 code=404 reason="Not Found" headers=0 consumed=26
empty reason after space: Done version=Http11 code=204 reason="" headers=0 consumed=17
no reason and no space: Done version=Http11 code=204 reason="" headers=0 consumed=16
reason with spaces: Done version=Http11 code=418 reason="I am a teapot" headers=0 consumed=30

== status line rejects ==
truncated mid-line (no CRLF yet): NeedMore
truncated: line ends before the code: Bad BadStatusLine
truncated: two-digit code: Bad BadStatusLine
code is not digits: Bad BadStatusLine
no space after version: Bad BadStatusLine
junk before the reason: Bad BadStatusLine
not HTTP at all: Bad BadStatusLine
binary junk (a TLS record header): Bad BadStatusLine
http/2: Bad BadVersion
http/0.9: Bad BadVersion
bare LF in reason: Bad BadStatusLine
bare CR in reason: Bad BadStatusLine
leading CRLF is NOT skipped: Bad BadStatusLine

== header block: the same grammar as a request head ==
two fields: Done version=Http11 code=200 reason="OK" headers=2 consumed=46
field with no colon: Bad BadField
space before colon: Bad BadField
obs-fold continuation: Bad BadField
empty field name: Bad BadField
head not terminated: NeedMore
head over 64 KiB: Bad HeadTooLarge
no CRLF anywhere, over cap: Bad HeadTooLarge

== consumed threads to the body ==
body starts at 38: "hello"

== response framing ==
no framing fields -> until close: BodyUntilClose
content-length: BodyLength 7
chunked: BodyChunked
204 with a content-length: BodyNone
304 with a content-length: BodyNone
100 continue: BodyNone
199 is still 1xx: BodyNone
200 is not: BodyLength 4
content-length AND chunked: BodyInvalid BadFraming
unknown transfer coding: BodyInvalid BadFraming
two disagreeing content-lengths: BodyInvalid BadFraming

== url ==
http://example.com -> Http host=example.com port=80 target="/" host-field="example.com"
https://example.com -> Https host=example.com port=443 target="/" host-field="example.com"
https://example.com/ -> Https host=example.com port=443 target="/" host-field="example.com"
http://example.com/a/b?q=1 -> Http host=example.com port=80 target="/a/b?q=1" host-field="example.com"
http://example.com?q=1 -> Http host=example.com port=80 target="/?q=1" host-field="example.com"
http://example.com/a#frag -> Http host=example.com port=80 target="/a" host-field="example.com"
http://example.com/a?q=1#frag -> Http host=example.com port=80 target="/a?q=1" host-field="example.com"
http://example.com:8080/a -> Http host=example.com port=8080 target="/a" host-field="example.com:8080"
https://example.com:443/a -> Https host=example.com port=443 target="/a" host-field="example.com"
https://example.com:8443/a -> Https host=example.com port=8443 target="/a" host-field="example.com:8443"
HTTPS://Example.COM/a -> Https host=Example.COM port=443 target="/a" host-field="Example.COM"
http://[::1]:9000/a -> Http host=::1 port=9000 target="/a" host-field="[::1]:9000"
http://[::1]/a -> Http host=::1 port=80 target="/a" host-field="[::1]"

== url rejects ==
/just/a/path -> Err MissingScheme
example.com/a -> Err MissingScheme
ftp://example.com/a -> Err UnsupportedScheme(<<102, 116, 112>>)
ws://example.com/a -> Err UnsupportedScheme(<<119, 115>>)
http:///a -> Err EmptyHost
http://:8080/a -> Err EmptyHost
http://example.com:/a -> Err BadPort(<<58>>)
http://example.com:0/a -> Err BadPort(<<58, 48>>)
http://example.com:65536/a -> Err BadPort(<<58, 54, 53, 53, 51, 54>>)
http://example.com:-1/a -> Err BadPort(<<58, 45, 49>>)
http://example.com:80x/a -> Err BadPort(<<58, 56, 48, 120>>)
http://user:pw@example.com/a -> Err UserInfoUnsupported
http://[::1/a -> Err UnclosedIpv6
http://[::1]x/a -> Err BadPort(<<120>>)

== client round trips (in-memory transport) ==
content-length body: 200 reason="OK" headers=1 body="hello"
content-length body, one byte per read: 200 reason="OK" headers=1 body="hello"
chunked body: 200 reason="OK" headers=1 body="hello world"
close-framed body: 200 reason="OK" headers=0 body="no framing fields here"
HEAD: content-length but no body: 200 reason="OK" headers=1 body=""
204 has no body whatever it says: 204 reason="No Content" headers=1 body=""
100 Continue before the real reply: 201 reason="Created" headers=1 body="hi"
two interim responses: 200 reason="OK" headers=1 body="hi"

== client round trips that must FAIL ==
body shorter than content-length: Err Transport(UnexpectedEof)
peer closes mid-head: Err Transport(UnexpectedEof)
peer closes with nothing at all: Err Transport(UnexpectedEof)
malformed status line: Err MalformedResponse(BadStatusLine)
header with no colon: Err MalformedResponse(BadField)
framing conflict: Err MalformedResponse(BadFraming)
chunked body with a lying size: Err MalformedResponse(BadFraming)

== the body budget ==
content-length over budget: Err BodyTooLarge(10)
content-length exactly at budget: 200 body="abcd"
close-framed body over budget: Err BodyTooLarge(64)

== what the client actually wrote ==
GET /: sent, got 200
  wrote: "GET / HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: example.com\r\nContent-Length: 0\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n"
GET with query and port: sent, got 200
  wrote: "GET /a?q=1 HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: example.com:8080\r\nContent-Length: 0\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n"
GET https default port omits it: sent, got 200
  wrote: "GET /a HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: example.com\r\nContent-Length: 0\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n"
GET ipv6 host is bracketed: sent, got 200
  wrote: "GET /a HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: [::1]:9000\r\nContent-Length: 0\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n"
POST with a body: sent, got 200
  wrote: "POST /e HTTP/1.1\r\nContent-Type: text/plain\r\nHost: example.com\r\nContent-Length: 2\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\nhi"
caller-set Content-Length is replaced: sent, got 200
  wrote: "POST /e HTTP/1.1\r\ncontent-length: 2\r\nHost: example.com\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\nhi"
caller-set Host is replaced: sent, got 200
  wrote: "GET /e HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: example.com\r\nContent-Length: 0\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n"
CRLF in a header value is refused: Err BadRequestHeaders
  wrote: ""
a header name that is not a token is refused: Err BadRequestHeaders
  wrote: ""

== url errors reach the client surface ==
client.get of a non-URL: Err BadUrl(MissingScheme)
client.get of ftp: Err BadUrl(
  UnsupportedScheme(<<102, 116, 112>>)
)
